			<m_pNoteText type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang16393{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Tahoma;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs16 E2E transformer is responsible for protecting safety-related data elements, by invoking the E2E Library. It is\par%0D
invoked by RTE. On the sender side, E2E transformer E2E-protects the data. On the\par%0D
receiver side, E2E transformer E2E-checks the data, providing the result of the E2Echecks through RTE to SW-C.\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</m_pNoteText>
		</CGIAnnotation>
